IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-interpretation`
IMPORT `ei2-nouns`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), ss 29 to 35: the words used in ss 30 to 33; disqualification for
-- misconduct or leaving without just cause; disentitlement for a suspension for misconduct, for leave without just
-- cause and for an anticipated loss of employment; the union exception. Piece ei2. Text: the unofficial plain-text
-- rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30. Seat: the claimant who lost or left work.
--
-- Relations (Hohfeld). ss 30 to 33 take away the claimant's claim to benefits: the Commission has a privilege not to
-- pay and the claimant has no claim (a no-right) for the weeks covered; s 35 is the claimant's immunity from the
-- operation of ss 30 and 33 in the one case it describes.
--
-- Judgments the Act leaves to a decider are BOOLEAN inputs: that the claimant had "no reasonable alternative" (s 29(c)),
-- that an employment, loss or leaving was "because of misconduct", that leaving was "without just cause". The
-- hours "required by section 7 or 7.1" are ei1's (out of range: sections 7 and 7.1, piece ei1) and are a NUMBER input.
--
-- Not applied here: s 35 is read as an exception to the "left or refused to accept" limbs of ss 30 and 33 only (fork
-- ei2-F5 in NOTES.md); s 31 (a suspension) and s 32 (a period of leave) are not a leaving or a refusal in those words.

§ `Section 29 - interpretation for sections 30 to 33`

-- (a) "employment refers to any employment of the claimant within their qualifying period or their benefit period".
-- The qualifying period (s 8) and the benefit period (ss 9 and 10) are ei1's (out of range: sections 8 to 10, piece ei1);
-- whether the employment is within one is a fact the caller states.
-- src:743 | 29 For the purposes of sections 30 to 33,
-- src:744 | (a) employment refers to any employment of the claimant within their qualifying period or their benefit period;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 29(a) (src:743-744)
GIVEN `the employment is within the claimant's qualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment is within the claimant's benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 29(a) the employment is an employment for the purposes of sections 30 to 33` IF
       `the employment is within the claimant's qualifying period`
    OR `the employment is within the claimant's benefit period`

-- (b) "loss of employment includes a suspension from employment, but does not include loss of, or suspension from,
-- employment on account of membership in, or lawful activity connected with, an association, organization or union
-- of workers". The ordinary loss of an employment is a fact the caller states; the definition adds suspension and
-- takes away the union reason.
-- src:743 | 29 For the purposes of sections 30 to 33,
-- src:745 | (b) loss of employment includes a suspension from employment, but does not include loss of, or suspension from, employment on account of membership in, or lawful activity connected with, an association, organization or union of workers;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 29(b) (src:743) (src:745)
GIVEN `the claimant lost the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant was suspended from the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on account of membership in, or lawful activity connected with, an association, organization or union of workers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 29(b) loss of employment` IF
        (`the claimant lost the employment` OR `the claimant was suspended from the employment`)
    AND (NOT `on account of membership in, or lawful activity connected with, an association, organization or union of workers`)

-- (b.1) "voluntarily leaving an employment includes (i) the refusal of employment offered as an alternative to an
-- anticipated loss of employment, ... (ii) the refusal to resume an employment, ... (iii) the refusal to continue in an
-- employment after the work, undertaking or business of the employer is transferred to another employer". The ordinary
-- voluntary leaving is a fact the caller states.
-- src:743 | 29 For the purposes of sections 30 to 33,
-- src:746 | (b.1) voluntarily leaving an employment includes
-- src:747 | (i) the refusal of employment offered as an alternative to an anticipated loss of employment, in which case the voluntary leaving occurs when the loss of employment occurs,
-- src:748 | (ii) the refusal to resume an employment, in which case the voluntary leaving occurs when the employment is supposed to be resumed, and
-- src:749 | (iii) the refusal to continue in an employment after the work, undertaking or business of the employer is transferred to another employer, in which case the voluntary leaving occurs when the work, undertaking or business is transferred; and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 29(b.1) (src:743) (src:746-749)
GIVEN `the claimant left the employment voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant refused employment offered as an alternative to an anticipated loss of employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant refused to resume the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant refused to continue in the employment after the work, undertaking or business of the employer was transferred to another employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 29(b.1) voluntarily leaving an employment` IF
       `the claimant left the employment voluntarily`
    OR `the claimant refused employment offered as an alternative to an anticipated loss of employment`
    OR `the claimant refused to resume the employment`
    OR `the claimant refused to continue in the employment after the work, undertaking or business of the employer was transferred to another employer`

-- The day on which the voluntary leaving occurs: (i) when the loss of employment occurs; (ii) when the employment is
-- supposed to be resumed; (iii) when the work, undertaking or business is transferred. For an ordinary voluntary
-- leaving the text gives no rule, and the day is the day the claimant left: NOTHING here, the caller uses that day.
-- src:746 | (b.1) voluntarily leaving an employment includes
-- src:747 | (i) the refusal of employment offered as an alternative to an anticipated loss of employment, in which case the voluntary leaving occurs when the loss of employment occurs,
-- src:748 | (ii) the refusal to resume an employment, in which case the voluntary leaving occurs when the employment is supposed to be resumed, and
-- src:749 | (iii) the refusal to continue in an employment after the work, undertaking or business of the employer is transferred to another employer, in which case the voluntary leaving occurs when the work, undertaking or business is transferred; and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 29(b.1) (src:746-749)
GIVEN `the claimant refused employment offered as an alternative to an anticipated loss of employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the loss of employment occurs` IS A DATE
      `the claimant refused to resume the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the employment is supposed to be resumed` IS A DATE
      `the claimant refused to continue in the employment after the work, undertaking or business of the employer was transferred to another employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the work, undertaking or business is transferred` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 29(b.1) the day on which a refusal counts as the voluntary leaving` IS
    BRANCH IF `the claimant refused employment offered as an alternative to an anticipated loss of employment` THEN JUST `the day on which the loss of employment occurs`
           IF `the claimant refused to resume the employment`                                              THEN JUST `the day on which the employment is supposed to be resumed`
           IF `the claimant refused to continue in the employment after the work, undertaking or business of the employer was transferred to another employer` THEN JUST `the day on which the work, undertaking or business is transferred`
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- (c) "just cause for voluntarily leaving an employment or taking leave from an employment exists if the claimant had
-- no reasonable alternative to leaving or taking leave, having regard to all the circumstances, including any of the
-- following". The test is "no reasonable alternative", a judgment. The fourteen items are circumstances to which regard
-- is had, not conditions that settle the question (fork ei2-F4 in NOTES.md).
-- src:750 | (c) just cause for voluntarily leaving an employment or taking leave from an employment exists if the claimant had no reasonable alternative to leaving or taking leave, having regard to all the circumstances, including any of the following:
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 29(c) (src:750)
GIVEN `the claimant had no reasonable alternative to leaving or taking leave, having regard to all the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 29(c) just cause for voluntarily leaving an employment or taking leave exists` IF
    `the claimant had no reasonable alternative to leaving or taking leave, having regard to all the circumstances`

-- The fourteen circumstances; (xiv) is "any other reasonable circumstances that are prescribed", which reg 51.1 (out of
-- range: Regulations s 51.1, piece er3) fills in: a BOOLEAN input. A TRUE answer means only that the Act names the
-- circumstance as one to have regard to.
-- src:751 | (i) sexual or other harassment,
-- src:752 | (ii) obligation to accompany a spouse, common-law partner or dependent child to another residence,
-- src:753 | (iii) discrimination on a prohibited ground of discrimination within the meaning of the Canadian Human Rights Act,
-- src:754 | (iv) working conditions that constitute a danger to health or safety,
-- src:755 | (v) obligation to care for a child or a member of the immediate family,
-- src:756 | (vi) reasonable assurance of another employment in the immediate future,
-- src:757 | (vii) significant modification of terms and conditions respecting wages or salary,
-- src:758 | (viii) excessive overtime work or refusal to pay for overtime work,
-- src:759 | (ix) significant changes in work duties,
-- src:760 | (x) antagonism with a supervisor if the claimant is not primarily responsible for the antagonism,
-- src:761 | (xi) practices of an employer that are contrary to law,
-- src:762 | (xii) discrimination with regard to employment because of membership in an association, organization or union of workers,
-- src:763 | (xiii) undue pressure by an employer on the claimant to leave their employment, and
-- src:764 | (xiv) any other reasonable circumstances that are prescribed.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 29(c)(i) to (xiv) (src:751-764)
GIVEN `sexual or other harassment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `obligation to accompany a spouse, common-law partner or dependent child to another residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `discrimination on a prohibited ground of discrimination within the meaning of the Canadian Human Rights Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `working conditions that constitute a danger to health or safety` IS A BOOLEAN
      `obligation to care for a child or a member of the immediate family` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasonable assurance of another employment in the immediate future` IS A BOOLEAN
      `significant modification of terms and conditions respecting wages or salary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `excessive overtime work or refusal to pay for overtime work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `significant changes in work duties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `antagonism with a supervisor if the claimant is not primarily responsible for the antagonism` IS A BOOLEAN
      `practices of an employer that are contrary to law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `discrimination with regard to employment because of membership in an association, organization or union of workers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `undue pressure by an employer on the claimant to leave their employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any other reasonable circumstances that are prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 29(c) one of the circumstances listed in the Act is present` IF
       `sexual or other harassment`
    OR `obligation to accompany a spouse, common-law partner or dependent child to another residence`
    OR `discrimination on a prohibited ground of discrimination within the meaning of the Canadian Human Rights Act`
    OR `working conditions that constitute a danger to health or safety`
    OR `obligation to care for a child or a member of the immediate family`
    OR `reasonable assurance of another employment in the immediate future`
    OR `significant modification of terms and conditions respecting wages or salary`
    OR `excessive overtime work or refusal to pay for overtime work`
    OR `significant changes in work duties`
    OR `antagonism with a supervisor if the claimant is not primarily responsible for the antagonism`
    OR `practices of an employer that are contrary to law`
    OR `discrimination with regard to employment because of membership in an association, organization or union of workers`
    OR `undue pressure by an employer on the claimant to leave their employment`
    OR `any other reasonable circumstances that are prescribed`

§ `Section 30 - disqualification for misconduct or leaving without just cause`

-- (1): "A claimant is disqualified from receiving any benefits if the claimant lost any employment because of their
-- misconduct or voluntarily left any employment without just cause, unless (a) the claimant has, since losing or
-- leaving the employment, been employed in insurable employment for the number of hours required by section 7 or
-- 7.1 to qualify to receive benefits; or (b) the claimant is disentitled under sections 31 to 33 in relation to the
-- employment." Section 35 takes the leaving limb away in its one case (fork ei2-F5).
-- src:765 | Disqualification — misconduct or leaving without just cause
-- src:766 | 30 (1) A claimant is disqualified from receiving any benefits if the claimant lost any employment because of their misconduct or voluntarily left any employment without just cause, unless
-- src:767 | (a) the claimant has, since losing or leaving the employment, been employed in insurable employment for the number of hours required by section 7 or 7.1 to qualify to receive benefits; or
-- src:768 | (b) the claimant is disentitled under sections 31 to 33 in relation to the employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 30(1) (src:765-768)
GIVEN `the claimant lost any employment because of their misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant voluntarily left any employment without just cause` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 35 protects the claimant from being disqualified only because the claimant left or refused to accept employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the hours of insurable employment the claimant has had since losing or leaving the employment` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of hours required by section 7 or 7.1 to qualify to receive benefits` IS A NUMBER
      `the claimant is disentitled under sections 31 to 33 in relation to the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 30(1) the claimant is disqualified from receiving any benefits` IF
        (   `the claimant lost any employment because of their misconduct`
         OR (`the claimant voluntarily left any employment without just cause` AND (NOT `section 35 protects the claimant from being disqualified only because the claimant left or refused to accept employment`)))
    AND (NOT (`the hours of insurable employment the claimant has had since losing or leaving the employment` AT LEAST `the number of hours required by section 7 or 7.1 to qualify to receive benefits`))
    AND (NOT `the claimant is disentitled under sections 31 to 33 in relation to the employment`)

-- (2), (3), (4): which weeks the disqualification covers. A week is identified by the date of its Sunday. The benefit
-- period and the waiting period are ei1's (out of range: sections 10 and 13, piece ei1): `Period of days` inputs.
-- (2) "The disqualification is for each week of the claimant's benefit period following the waiting period and, for
-- greater certainty, the length of the disqualification is not affected by any subsequent loss of employment by the
-- claimant during the benefit period."
-- src:769 | Length of disqualification
-- src:770 | (2) The disqualification is for each week of the claimant’s benefit period following the waiting period and, for greater certainty, the length of the disqualification is not affected by any subsequent loss of employment by the claimant during the benefit period.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 30(2) (src:769-770)
GIVEN `the Sunday of the week` IS A DATE
      `the claimant's benefit period` IS A `Period of days`
      `the waiting period` IS A `Period of days`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 30(2) the week is a week of the benefit period following the waiting period` IF
        `the day` `the Sunday of the week` `falls within` `the claimant's benefit period`
    AND `the Sunday of the week` AT LEAST (`the waiting period`'s `last day of the period` PLUS 1)

-- (3) "If the event giving rise to the disqualification occurs during a benefit period of the claimant, the
-- disqualification does not include any week in that benefit period before the week in which the event occurs."
-- src:771 | Not retroactive
-- src:772 | (3) If the event giving rise to the disqualification occurs during a benefit period of the claimant, the disqualification does not include any week in that benefit period before the week in which the event occurs.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 30(3) (src:771-772)
GIVEN `the event giving rise to the disqualification occurs during a benefit period of the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the event` IS A DATE
      `the Sunday of the week` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 30(3) the week is not a week before the week in which the event occurs` IF
       (NOT `the event giving rise to the disqualification occurs during a benefit period of the claimant`)
    OR `the Sunday of the week` AT LEAST `s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` `the day of the event`

-- (4) "Despite subsection (6), the disqualification is suspended during any week for which the claimant is otherwise
-- entitled to special benefits." (The words "Despite subsection (6)" are the text's; see NOTES.md, finding 3.)
-- src:773 | Suspension
-- src:774 | (4) Despite subsection (6), the disqualification is suspended during any week for which the claimant is otherwise entitled to special benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 30(4) (src:773-774)
GIVEN `the claimant is otherwise entitled to benefits for the week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reason for those benefits` IS A `Reason for benefits`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 30(4) the disqualification is suspended for the week` IF
        `the claimant is otherwise entitled to benefits for the week`
    AND `s 2(1) special benefits` `the reason for those benefits`

-- src:769 | Length of disqualification
-- src:770 | (2) The disqualification is for each week of the claimant’s benefit period following the waiting period and, for greater certainty, the length of the disqualification is not affected by any subsequent loss of employment by the claimant during the benefit period.
-- src:771 | Not retroactive
-- src:772 | (3) If the event giving rise to the disqualification occurs during a benefit period of the claimant, the disqualification does not include any week in that benefit period before the week in which the event occurs.
-- src:773 | Suspension
-- src:774 | (4) Despite subsection (6), the disqualification is suspended during any week for which the claimant is otherwise entitled to special benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 30(2), s 30(3), s 30(4) (src:769-774)
GIVEN `the claimant is disqualified under subsection 30(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the week is a week of the benefit period following the waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the week is not a week before the week in which the event occurs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disqualification is suspended for the week` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 30(2) to (4) the week is a week of disqualification` IF
        `the claimant is disqualified under subsection 30(1)`
    AND `the week is a week of the benefit period following the waiting period`
    AND `the week is not a week before the week in which the event occurs`
    AND (NOT `the disqualification is suspended for the week`)

-- (5) "If a claimant who has lost or left an employment as described in subsection (1) makes an initial claim for
-- benefits, the following hours may not be used to qualify under section 7 or 7.1 to receive benefits: (a) hours of
-- insurable employment from that or any other employment before the employment was lost or left; and (b) hours of
-- insurable employment in any employment that the claimant subsequently loses or leaves, as described in
-- subsection (1)." "As described in subsection (1)" is the loss or leaving the subsection names, whatever the unless-limbs say; the caller states
-- whether it applies (fork ei2-F14). The hours that may be used are the total less those two groups; NOTHING when the subsection does not
-- apply, or when the two groups together exceed the total (the figures cannot be right).
-- src:775 | Restriction on qualifying for benefits
-- src:776 | (5) If a claimant who has lost or left an employment as described in subsection (1) makes an initial claim for benefits, the following hours may not be used to qualify under section 7 or 7.1 to receive benefits:
-- src:777 | (a) hours of insurable employment from that or any other employment before the employment was lost or left; and
-- src:778 | (b) hours of insurable employment in any employment that the claimant subsequently loses or leaves, as described in subsection (1).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 30(5) (src:775-778)
GIVEN `the claimant has lost or left an employment as described in subsection 30(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant makes an initial claim for benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total hours of insurable employment the claimant has had` IS A NUMBER
      `the hours of insurable employment from that or any other employment before the employment was lost or left` IS A NUMBER
      `the hours of insurable employment in any employment that the claimant subsequently loses or leaves, as described in subsection 30(1)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 30(5) the hours that may be used to qualify under section 7 or 7.1` IS
    IF     `the claimant has lost or left an employment as described in subsection 30(1)`
       AND `the claimant makes an initial claim for benefits`
       AND (`the total hours of insurable employment the claimant has had` AT LEAST (`the hours of insurable employment from that or any other employment before the employment was lost or left` PLUS `the hours of insurable employment in any employment that the claimant subsequently loses or leaves, as described in subsection 30(1)`))
    THEN JUST (`the total hours of insurable employment the claimant has had` MINUS (`the hours of insurable employment from that or any other employment before the employment was lost or left` PLUS `the hours of insurable employment in any employment that the claimant subsequently loses or leaves, as described in subsection 30(1)`))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (6) "No hours of insurable employment in any employment that a claimant loses or leaves, as described in subsection
-- (1), may be used for the purpose of determining the maximum number of weeks of benefits under subsection 12(2) or the
-- claimant's rate of weekly benefits under section 14." (Sections 12(2) and 14 are piece ei1's.)
-- src:779 | Restriction on number of weeks and rate of benefits
-- src:780 | (6) No hours of insurable employment in any employment that a claimant loses or leaves, as described in subsection (1), may be used for the purpose of determining the maximum number of weeks of benefits under subsection 12(2) or the claimant’s rate of weekly benefits under section 14.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 30(6) (src:779-780)
GIVEN `the total hours of insurable employment the claimant has had` IS A NUMBER
      `the hours of insurable employment in any employment that the claimant loses or leaves, as described in subsection 30(1)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 30(6) the hours that may be used to determine the maximum weeks and the rate of weekly benefits` IS
    IF `the total hours of insurable employment the claimant has had` AT LEAST `the hours of insurable employment in any employment that the claimant loses or leaves, as described in subsection 30(1)`
    THEN JUST (`the total hours of insurable employment the claimant has had` MINUS `the hours of insurable employment in any employment that the claimant loses or leaves, as described in subsection 30(1)`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (7) "For greater certainty, but subject to paragraph (1)(a), a claimant may be disqualified under subsection (1)
-- even if the claimant's last employment before their claim for benefits was not lost or left as described in that
-- subsection and regardless of whether their claim is an initial claim for benefits." Declaratory: s 30(1) above has
-- no input for either fact, so it already gives that result. It is recorded as the test it is, in
-- ei2-tests-leaving-and-misconduct.l4 (phrasebook 10.1).

§ `Section 31 - disentitlement for a suspension for misconduct`

-- "A claimant who is suspended from their employment because of their misconduct is not entitled to receive benefits
-- until (a) the period of suspension expires; (b) the claimant loses or voluntarily leaves the employment; or (c) the
-- claimant, after the beginning of the period of suspension, accumulates with another employer the number of hours of
-- insurable employment required by section 7 or 7.1 to qualify to receive benefits." Each "until" is a fact about the
-- day in question: has it happened by that day (fork ei2-F13).
-- src:783 | Disentitlement — suspension for misconduct
-- src:784 | 31 A claimant who is suspended from their employment because of their misconduct is not entitled to receive benefits until
-- src:785 | (a) the period of suspension expires;
-- src:786 | (b) the claimant loses or voluntarily leaves the employment; or
-- src:787 | (c) the claimant, after the beginning of the period of suspension, accumulates with another employer the number of hours of insurable employment required by section 7 or 7.1 to qualify to receive benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 31 (src:783-787)
GIVEN `the claimant is suspended from their employment because of their misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period of suspension has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has lost or voluntarily left the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the hours of insurable employment accumulated with another employer after the beginning of the period of suspension` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of hours required by section 7 or 7.1 to qualify to receive benefits` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 31 the claimant is not entitled to receive benefits` IF
        `the claimant is suspended from their employment because of their misconduct`
    AND (NOT `the period of suspension has expired`)
    AND (NOT `the claimant has lost or voluntarily left the employment`)
    AND (NOT (`the hours of insurable employment accumulated with another employer after the beginning of the period of suspension` AT LEAST `the number of hours required by section 7 or 7.1 to qualify to receive benefits`))

§ `Section 32 - disentitlement for a period of leave without just cause`

-- (1) "A claimant who voluntarily takes a period of leave from their employment without just cause is not entitled to
-- receive benefits if, before or after the beginning of the period of leave, (a) the period of leave was authorized by
-- the employer; and (b) the claimant and the employer agreed as to the day on which the claimant would resume employment."
-- src:788 | Disentitlement — period of leave without just cause
-- src:789 | 32 (1) A claimant who voluntarily takes a period of leave from their employment without just cause is not entitled to receive benefits if, before or after the beginning of the period of leave,
-- src:790 | (a) the period of leave was authorized by the employer; and
-- src:791 | (b) the claimant and the employer agreed as to the day on which the claimant would resume employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 32(1) (src:788-791)
GIVEN `the claimant voluntarily takes a period of leave from their employment without just cause` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period of leave was authorized by the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant and the employer agreed as to the day on which the claimant would resume employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 32(1) the claimant who takes leave is disentitled` IF
        `the claimant voluntarily takes a period of leave from their employment without just cause`
    AND `the period of leave was authorized by the employer`
    AND `the claimant and the employer agreed as to the day on which the claimant would resume employment`

-- (2) "The disentitlement lasts until the claimant (a) resumes the employment; (b) loses or voluntarily leaves the
-- employment; or (c) after the beginning of the period of leave, accumulates with another employer the number of
-- hours of insurable employment required by section 7 or 7.1 to qualify to receive benefits." Each event is a fact about the day
-- in question (fork ei2-F13).
-- src:792 | Duration of disentitlement
-- src:793 | (2) The disentitlement lasts until the claimant
-- src:794 | (a) resumes the employment;
-- src:795 | (b) loses or voluntarily leaves the employment; or
-- src:796 | (c) after the beginning of the period of leave, accumulates with another employer the number of hours of insurable employment required by section 7 or 7.1 to qualify to receive benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 32(2) (src:792-796)
GIVEN `the claimant has resumed the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has lost or voluntarily left the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the hours of insurable employment accumulated with another employer after the beginning of the period of leave` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of hours required by section 7 or 7.1 to qualify to receive benefits` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 32(2) the disentitlement has ended` IF
       `the claimant has resumed the employment`
    OR `the claimant has lost or voluntarily left the employment`
    OR `the hours of insurable employment accumulated with another employer after the beginning of the period of leave` AT LEAST `the number of hours required by section 7 or 7.1 to qualify to receive benefits`

§ `Section 33 - disentitlement for an anticipated loss of employment`

-- (1) "A claimant is not entitled to receive benefits if the claimant loses an employment because of their misconduct
-- or voluntarily leaves without just cause within three weeks before (a) the expiration of a term of employment, in the
-- case of employment for a set term; or (b) the day on which the claimant is to be laid off according to a notice
-- already given by the employer to the claimant." Three weeks are 21 days; the loss or leaving is "within" them if it
-- falls on or after the 21st day before the end day and on or before the end day (fork ei2-F6).
-- src:797 | Disentitlement — anticipated loss of employment
-- src:798 | 33 (1) A claimant is not entitled to receive benefits if the claimant loses an employment because of their misconduct or voluntarily leaves without just cause within three weeks before
-- src:799 | (a) the expiration of a term of employment, in the case of employment for a set term; or
-- src:800 | (b) the day on which the claimant is to be laid off according to a notice already given by the employer to the claimant.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 33(1) (src:797-800)
GIVEN `the claimant loses an employment because of their misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant voluntarily leaves without just cause` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 35 protects the claimant from being disentitled only because the claimant left or refused to accept employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the claimant lost or left the employment` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the term of a set-term employment expires, if the employment was for a set term` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the claimant is to be laid off according to a notice already given by the employer, if such a notice was given` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 33(1) the claimant is not entitled to receive benefits` IF
        (   `the claimant loses an employment because of their misconduct`
         OR (`the claimant voluntarily leaves without just cause` AND (NOT `section 35 protects the claimant from being disentitled only because the claimant left or refused to accept employment`)))
    AND (   `the claimant lost or left within three weeks before` `the day on which the claimant lost or left the employment` `the day on which the term of a set-term employment expires, if the employment was for a set term`
         OR `the claimant lost or left within three weeks before` `the day on which the claimant lost or left the employment` `the day on which the claimant is to be laid off according to a notice already given by the employer, if such a notice was given`)
    WHERE
        `the claimant lost or left within three weeks before` lostOrLeft endDay MEANS
            CONSIDER endDay
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST e  THEN lostOrLeft AT LEAST (e MINUS `weeks as days` 3) AND lostOrLeft AT MOST e

-- (2) "The disentitlement lasts until the expiration of the term of employment or the day on which the claimant was
-- to be laid off." The end day counts (fork ei2-F7): the claimant is disentitled on every day up to and including it.
-- src:801 | Duration of disentitlement
-- src:802 | (2) The disentitlement lasts until the expiration of the term of employment or the day on which the claimant was to be laid off.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 33(2) (src:801-802)
GIVEN `the claimant is not entitled under subsection 33(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the term expired or the claimant was to be laid off` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 33(2) the disentitlement is still in force on the day` IF
        `the claimant is not entitled under subsection 33(1)`
    AND `the day in question` AT MOST `the day on which the term expired or the claimant was to be laid off`

§ `Section 34 - suspension of the disentitlement`

-- "A disentitlement under sections 31 to 33 is suspended during any week for which the claimant is otherwise entitled
-- to special benefits." Not a disentitlement at all, nothing to suspend: FALSE here is correct.
-- src:803 | Suspension of disentitlement
-- src:804 | 34 A disentitlement under sections 31 to 33 is suspended during any week for which the claimant is otherwise entitled to special benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 34 (src:803-804)
GIVEN `the claimant is disentitled under section 31, 32 or 33` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is otherwise entitled to benefits for the week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reason for those benefits` IS A `Reason for benefits`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 34 the disentitlement is suspended for the week` IF
        `the claimant is disentitled under section 31, 32 or 33`
    AND `the claimant is otherwise entitled to benefits for the week`
    AND `s 2(1) special benefits` `the reason for those benefits`

§ `Section 35 - the union exception`

-- "Notwithstanding anything in this Part, no claimant is disqualified or disentitled under sections 30 to 33 from
-- receiving benefits only because the claimant left or refused to accept employment if, by remaining in or accepting
-- the employment, the claimant would lose the right (a) to become or refrain from becoming a member of an association,
-- organization or union of workers; or (b) to continue to be a member and to observe the lawful rules of an
-- association, organization or union of workers." MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE when the exception applies, NOTHING
-- otherwise (the section then says nothing).
-- src:805 | Exception
-- src:806 | 35 Notwithstanding anything in this Part, no claimant is disqualified or disentitled under sections 30 to 33 from receiving benefits only because the claimant left or refused to accept employment if, by remaining in or accepting the employment, the claimant would lose the right
-- src:807 | (a) to become or refrain from becoming a member of an association, organization or union of workers; or
-- src:808 | (b) to continue to be a member and to observe the lawful rules of an association, organization or union of workers.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 35 (src:805-808)
GIVEN `the only reason for the disqualification or disentitlement is that the claimant left or refused to accept employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by remaining in or accepting the employment the claimant would lose the right to become or refrain from becoming a member of an association, organization or union of workers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by remaining in or accepting the employment the claimant would lose the right to continue to be a member and to observe the lawful rules of an association, organization or union of workers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 35 the claimant is not disqualified or disentitled under sections 30 to 33` IS
    IF     `the only reason for the disqualification or disentitlement is that the claimant left or refused to accept employment`
       AND (   `by remaining in or accepting the employment the claimant would lose the right to become or refrain from becoming a member of an association, organization or union of workers`
            OR `by remaining in or accepting the employment the claimant would lose the right to continue to be a member and to observe the lawful rules of an association, organization or union of workers`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
